  reveal at the end of every episode this  is  the dumbest show ever and i love it  episode 31  the name of the episode is limit breaker  broly  is resurrected let that sink in so as  food tangos with two vegitos that have  lasted in their respective forms longer  in this instance than the entire series  combined it feels like  suddenly transports them or conjures a  floating fortress in space beneath a big  tree  when broly suddenly attacks remember  this story began with goku playing with  a bird and now it's  i have legitimately no more words to  accurately convey my bewilderment and  shock over how stupid this is  so let's turn to the dictionary this is  inscrutable beyond any measure okay i  feel better  so fu restores the tree to broly's  unheralded and sudden arrival  time to deal with that now i guess  episode 32 so  blue vegito keeps broly busy while super  saiyan 4 vegito fights foo  that's most of the episode but perhaps  the strangest thing happens in the  series yet  it doesn't end in a cheap fashion like  with a transformation or a new character  revelation instead the hook is  narratively driven  sort of suddenly goku awakens outside  the capsule corp totally fine  how did he get there how will he help  his friends tune in next time  episode 33 all right it's next time so  apparently the last episode was the end  of the last arc and this is the start of  a brand new one  it seems like this story does the exact  opposite of super it connects arcs but  not episodes within an arc interestingly  however it's revealed that foo was  successful and that goku is now in a  universe that foo  created as he's hunted down through the  streets of west city that's sort of cool  i guess  that is until i realized that frieza and  mecca cooler are the ones chasing after  him so  hearts shows up and i'm not even  remotely kidding here i didn't recognize  him without his sunglasses apparently  he's a good guy now i like how ultra  instinct is being used here in the  setting also but  yeah mask goku shows up no idea what  that means next  episode episode 34 the animation and  direction in this one is  noticeably different it's not the same  shots over and over again or the same  boring layouts and cuts of animation  there's a different person behind the  wheel of this one and it's abundantly  clear so  this evil goku is using the dark dragon  balls to empower and control frieza and  cooler and then  broly shows up out of nowhere making  loud and annoying noises again  reminding me that yes i am indeed  watching super dragon ball heroes  everyone disappears and we get a new  goal collect all the dragon balls to  make a wish  all the while vegeta's above them about  to fight comber and turles  episode 35 there's again more fighting  in this episode with some  super saiyan rose and super saiyan blue  goku not to mention turtles and cumber  going at it but  the highlight for me has to be the  instances where the series suddenly  shifts as turles encourages vegeta to  try and embrace his darker side  through which we're shown reanimated  versions of iconic scenes from the  original series and for a brief moment i  remembered what it was like to watch  dragon ball and enjoy it in a moment  where i genuinely felt as though  vegeta's character was treated with some  level of intelligence by referring to  his past to inform his present  and i say that totally ignoring how dumb  it looked with the black and blue aura  by the way  but the reason i draw attention to this  at all is because  it made me stop to think having spent  the last year and a half  reading and reviewing some of the best  stories in shonen returning to the  dragon ball franchise by way of super  dragon ball heroes was  a less than satisfying affair i mean  it's sort of like returning to watch  disney by way of the live-action mulan  movie it's trash and it's unanimously  recognized by the majority as such but  even with that in mind this show  while reminding me of what the series  was has planted a few seeds of doubt  dragon ball was my favorite story for  most of my life  and was one that has given me the life  that i have today i wouldn't have a  channel if not for that very series  the colorful and lighthearted characters  as well as the iconic moments throughout  will always hold a special place in my  heart but having watched all of those  episodes of super dragon ball heroes  it's left me wondering does the original  dragon ball hold up after  all these years is it as good as i  remember it to be  or has the last year full of reviewing  the very best shonen has to offer  changed my perception on the series that  started it all for me  so i've got an idea it's been a very  long time since i consistently uploaded  dragon ball content and the early  portion of the series is one of the most  underrated aspects of the story with the  most casual fans never having even seen  it  so seeing as i've reviewed all of dragon  ball gt and dragon ball super  how about i finish this series right  starting next week i totally not mark  i'm returning to dragon ball  to review akira toriyama's worldwide  smash hit  i'll see you there  [Music]  you
 

